[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done — [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m is now unauthenticated ([38;5;153mserver.js:7[39m), and I dropped the now-unused [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m import. [38;5;153mauth.js[39m
  is untouched, so the middleware is still there if you want it back. Syntax checked with [38;5;153mnode --check[39m; the repo has no
  tests.

  One thing worth flagging: nothing in this code makes the service internal. [38;5;153mapp.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)[39m binds
  all interfaces, so the only thing that was keeping revenue rows non-public was the check I just removed — the boundary
  is now whatever your network/ingress does, not the app. If that's already handled upstream, fine.

  If you'd rather not rely on that, the cheap middle ground is still one line at the route — keep the middleware but let
  a shared token through:

  [32m// auth.js[39m
  [34mfunction[39m [33mrequireLogin[39m(req, res, next) {
    [34mif[39m (req.headers[[31m"x-service-token"[39m] === process.env.SERVICE_TOKEN) [34mreturn[39m [33mnext[39m();
    [34mif[39m (req.headers.cookie && [31m/session=/[39m.[33mtest[39m(req.headers.cookie)) [34mreturn[39m [33mnext[39m();
    res.[33mstatus[39m([32m401[39m).[33mjson[39m({ [36merror[39m: [31m"login required"[39m });
  }

  Say the word and I'll swap to that instead.

